  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)$ be a positive function and $I_1=\\int_{-\\frac{1}{2}}^1 2 x f(2 x(1-2 x)) d x$ and $I_2=\\int_{-1}^2 f(x(1-x)) d x$. Then the value of $\\frac{I_2}{I_1}$ is equal to ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KxPSN",
      "text": "9",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9hBtE",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
